      },
      "notes": "Pharmacokinetic parameters of voriconazole after doses of 10 to 80 mg/kg by oral gavage\nS03 | DOI 10.1128/AAC.00606-10 | Table 2 (checked against the PDF)\nFemale CD-1 mice 20-22 g, 4-5 weeks, NON-neutropenic; disseminated aspergillosis (A. fumigatus AZN 8196 i.v.). Voriconazole oral solution by gavage once daily, 10, 40 or 80 mg/kg, from 24 h after infection. PK blood sampled on DAY 2 OF TREATMENT (methods: \"immediately before administration of voriconazole and at 0, 0.5, 1, 2, 4, 6, 9, and 24 h postdosing\"; text: \"8 time points\"), 3 mice per time point, lithium-heparin plasma, HPLC-fluorescence, LLOQ 0.01 mg/liter for low concentrations.\nNo footnotes. The fAUC column unit is printed as \"mg·h/liter·kg\", the same as the dose-normalized AUC column. Text: \"The AUC normalized to a dose of 10 mg/kg resulted in ratios of 0.31, 1.75, and 3.68\"; \"Clearance decreased with increasing doses, showing nonlinearity.\"\nUnbound fraction by ultrafiltration of pooled 1, 2, 4 h plasma (n = 3 per dosing arm): \"26.51%, 33.28%, and 30.59% for the 10-, 40-, and 80-mg/kg groups\"; \"geometric mean unbound voriconazole fraction for all groups combined (n = 9) was 29.97% (95% confidence interval [95% CI], 27.56 to 32.59%)\". Discussion: \"29.87% (standard deviation, 2.9%)\".",
      "column_map": {
        "c001_treatment_dose_mg_kg": "Treatment dose (mg/kg)",
