        "quote": "Female CD-1 mice 20-22 g, 4-5 weeks, NON-neutropenic; disseminated aspergillosis (A. fumigatus AZN 8196 i.v.). Voriconazole oral solution by gavage once daily, 10, 40 or 80 mg/kg, from 24 h after infection. PK blood sampled on DAY 2 OF TREATMENT (methods: \"immediately before administration of voriconazole and at 0, 0.5, 1, 2, 4, 6, 9, and 24 h postdosing\"; text: \"8 time points\"), 3 mice per time point, lithium-heparin plasma, HPLC-fluorescence, LLOQ 0.01 mg/liter for low concentrations."
      },
      {
        "source": "F0003:S1:T2:A20",
        "quote": "No footnotes. The fAUC column unit is printed as \"mg·h/liter·kg\", the same as the dose-normalized AUC column. Text: \"The AUC normalized to a dose of 10 mg/kg resulted in ratios of 0.31, 1.75, and 3.68\"; \"Clearance decreased with increasing doses, showing nonlinearity.\""
      },
      {
        "source": "F0003:S1:T2:A21",
